<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>Documentation — The Agent Kit | Jay Framework</title>
  <meta name="description" content="The Jay Stack Agent Kit — documentation written for AI agents, readable by humans. Role-specific guides for Designer, Developer, Plugin Developer, and DevOps.">
  <script type="application/jay-data" contract="./page.jay-contract"></script>
  <script type="application/jay-headfull" src="../../components/site-header/site-header" names="SiteHeader" contract="../../components/site-header/site-header.jay-contract"></script>
  <script type="application/jay-headfull" src="../../components/site-footer/site-footer" names="SiteFooter" contract="../../components/site-footer/site-footer.jay-contract"></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles/theme.css" />
  <style>
    body {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    /* ── Hero ── */
    .docs-hero {
      position: relative;
      padding: 96px 0; /* design-system: allow */
      padding-top: 160px; /* design-system: allow */
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .docs-hero-grid {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      background-image:
        linear-gradient(rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.05) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.05) 1px, transparent 1px);
      background-size: 40px 40px;
      opacity: 0.3;
      z-index: 0;
    }
    .docs-hero-content {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .docs-hero-badge {
      display: inline-block;
      background: rgba(165, 231, 255, 0.1);
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: 4px 12px;
      border-radius: 9999px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    .docs-hero-headline {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px);
      line-height: 1.15;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(71, 214, 255, 0.5);
    }
    .docs-hero-subtitle {
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 28px;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 32px auto 0;
    }

    /* ── Intro ── */
    .docs-intro { background: var(--color-surface); }
    .docs-intro-content {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .docs-intro-content p {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 26px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    .docs-intro-content p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    /* ── What's in the Kit ── */
    .docs-kit { background: var(--color-surface-lowest); }
    .docs-kit-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .docs-kit-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    }
    .docs-kit-card {
      padding: 32px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    .docs-kit-card h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .docs-kit-card code {
      display: inline-block;
      background: var(--color-surface-high);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);
      padding: 0.15em 0.4em; /* design-system: allow */
      border-radius: 0.25rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.8em; /* design-system: allow */
    }
    .docs-kit-card p {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 24px;
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ── How Agents Use It ── */
    .docs-workflow { background: var(--color-surface); }
    .docs-workflow-steps {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .docs-workflow-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
    }
    .docs-workflow-step {
      padding: 28px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .docs-workflow-number {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 32px;
      height: 32px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.15);
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .docs-workflow-step h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .docs-workflow-step p {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 22px; /* design-system: allow */
      margin: 0;
    }
    .docs-workflow-step code {
      background: var(--color-surface-high);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);
      padding: 0.1em 0.35em; /* design-system: allow */
      border-radius: 0.25rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.85em; /* design-system: allow */
    }

    /* ── Role Cards ── */
    .docs-roles { background: var(--color-surface-lowest); }
    .docs-roles-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }
    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .docs-roles-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    }

    .docs-extensibility {
      margin-top: 48px;
      padding: 28px 32px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.1);
      background: rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.03);
    }
    .docs-extensibility p {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 24px;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .docs-extensibility strong {
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .glass-panel {
      background: rgba(10, 15, 30, 0.7);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.1);
      transition: border-color 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
    }
    .glass-panel:hover {
      border-color: rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.3);
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.05);
    }

    .docs-role-card {
      display: flex;
      gap: 20px;
      padding: 32px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
    }
    .docs-role-card:hover { text-decoration: none; }
    .docs-role-card--designer { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(176, 122, 237, 0.25), 0 0 4px rgba(176, 122, 237, 0.15); }
    .docs-role-card--developer { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(106, 191, 75, 0.25), 0 0 4px rgba(106, 191, 75, 0.15); }
    .docs-role-card--plugin { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(212, 149, 46, 0.25), 0 0 4px rgba(212, 149, 46, 0.15); }
    .docs-role-card--devops { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(91, 140, 201, 0.25), 0 0 4px rgba(91, 140, 201, 0.15); }
    .docs-role-card--contracts { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.2), 0 0 4px rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.1); }
    .docs-role-card--contracts { grid-column: 1 / -1; }

    .docs-role-icon {
      width: 64px;
      height: 64px;
      object-fit: contain;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .docs-role-body h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .docs-role-body p {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 24px;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .docs-role-body .docs-role-link {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    /* ── Hero Quick Links ── */
    .docs-hero-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    .docs-hero-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 8px 20px;
      border-radius: 9999px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(165, 231, 255, 0.15);
      background: rgba(165, 231, 255, 0.05);
      color: var(--color-text);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 500;
      transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
    }
    .docs-hero-link:hover {
      border-color: rgba(165, 231, 255, 0.35);
      background: rgba(165, 231, 255, 0.1);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .docs-hero-link img {
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
      object-fit: contain;
    }

    .section { padding: 96px 0; }
    .section-label {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 16px;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      letter-spacing: 0.4em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    /* ── Shimmer Pass ── */
    @keyframes shimmer-pass {
      0%   { background-position: -150% center; }
      15%  { background-position: -150% center; }
      35%  { background-position:  150% center; }
      100% { background-position:  150% center; }
    }
    .shimmer-wrap {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
    }
    .shimmer-base {
      color: inherit;
    }
    .shimmer-shine {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      background: linear-gradient(
        105deg,
        transparent 35%,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)  46%,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95) 50%,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)  54%,
        transparent 65%
      );
      background-size: 200% auto;
      background-repeat: no-repeat;
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      background-clip: text;
      color: transparent;
      text-shadow: none;
      animation: shimmer-pass 5s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page-root">
    <jay:SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <section class="docs-hero">
        <div class="docs-hero-grid"></div>
        <div class="container">
          <div class="docs-hero-content">
            <span class="docs-hero-badge">DOCUMENTATION</span>
            <h1 class="docs-hero-headline"><span class="shimmer-wrap"><span class="shimmer-base">The Agent Kit</span><span class="shimmer-shine" aria-hidden="true">The Agent Kit</span></span></h1>
            <p class="docs-hero-subtitle">Documentation written for AI agents, readable by humans. The Agent Kit tells each agent exactly what it can do, what files to touch, and what patterns to follow.</p>
            <div class="docs-hero-links">
              <a class="docs-hero-link" href="/docs/designer/instructions"><img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_ebd9e460d96049b195b5ef0b340cffc8~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_24,h_24/file.webp" alt="" width="20" height="20" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">Designer</a>
              <a class="docs-hero-link" href="/docs/developer/instructions"><img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_838a1a4885714dae9579fe0b4d1a2293~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_24,h_24/file.webp" alt="" width="20" height="20" loading="eager">Developer</a>
              <a class="docs-hero-link" href="/docs/plugin/instructions"><img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_e235dbf4943c4208aba88b4ed6ddd402~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_24,h_24/file.webp" alt="" width="20" height="20" loading="eager">Plugin</a>
              <a class="docs-hero-link" href="/docs/devops/instructions"><img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_eaf3402bcc7c4fc784b5ae848a04af28~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_24,h_24/file.webp" alt="" width="20" height="20" loading="eager">DevOps</a>
              <a class="docs-hero-link" href="/docs/contracts/guide"><img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_28d5b6b49bd14042b0eae9070028acf6~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_24,h_24/file.webp" alt="" width="20" height="20" loading="eager">Contracts</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section docs-intro">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="docs-intro-content">
            <span class="section-label">Overview</span>
            <h2 class="headline-lg" style="margin-top: 16px;">Why documentation for agents?</h2>
            <p>Traditional documentation explains concepts to humans. The Agent Kit takes a different approach — it provides <strong style="color: var(--color-text);">precise, specification-style instructions</strong> that AI agents can follow mechanically. Each role gets only the information relevant to its task, reducing hallucination and keeping agents within their boundaries.</p>
            <p>The Agent Kit is generated into the <code jay-design="allow" style="background: var(--color-surface-high); border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.875em;">agent-kit/</code> folder in your project root by running <code jay-design="allow" style="background: var(--color-surface-high); border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.875em;">jay-stack setup</code> followed by <code jay-design="allow" style="background: var(--color-surface-high); border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.875em;">jay-stack agent-kit</code>. Setup initializes your project's services; agent-kit then executes plugin generators against those live services to produce contracts that reflect your project's actual configured state. The result isn't generic documentation — it's a machine-readable manifest of what your project can do right now.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section docs-kit">
        <div class="container">
          <span class="section-label">Generated Artifacts</span>
          <h2 class="headline-lg" style="margin-top: 16px;">What's in the Kit</h2>
          <div class="docs-kit-grid">
            <div class="docs-kit-card glass-panel">
              <h3>Plugins Index</h3>
              <p><code>plugins-index.yaml</code></p>
              <p>The master discovery index. Lists every installed plugin's contracts, actions, services, contexts, routes, and CLI commands. This is how an agent finds out what's available — a single machine-readable manifest for the entire project.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-kit-card glass-panel">
              <h3>Materialized Contracts</h3>
              <p><code>materialized-contracts/</code></p>
              <p>Static contracts copied and dynamic contracts generated by executing plugin code against your project's live services. These aren't just docs — they're the actual tag schemas, data types, and props that agents bind to when writing templates and components.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-kit-card glass-panel">
              <h3>References</h3>
              <p><code>references/</code></p>
              <p>Plugin-generated reference data from your project's data sources — product catalogs, collection schemas, media indexes. Agents use these to produce realistic, grounded content instead of placeholder data.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-kit-card glass-panel">
              <h3>Role Guides</h3>
              <p><code>designer/</code> <code>developer/</code> <code>plugin/</code> <code>devops/</code></p>
              <p>Each role gets its own directory with an <code>INSTRUCTIONS.md</code> entry point and topic-specific guides — template syntax, routing, component state, deployment, and more. Agents read only the guides relevant to their role.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section docs-workflow">
        <div class="container">
          <span class="section-label">Discovery</span>
          <h2 class="headline-lg" style="margin-top: 16px;">How Agents Use It</h2>
          <div class="docs-workflow-steps">
            <div class="docs-workflow-step glass-panel">
              <div class="docs-workflow-number">1</div>
              <h3>Discover</h3>
              <p>Read <code>plugins-index.yaml</code> and the role's <code>INSTRUCTIONS.md</code> to learn what's available and how to work with it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-workflow-step glass-panel">
              <div class="docs-workflow-number">2</div>
              <h3>Understand</h3>
              <p>Read materialized contracts for exact tag schemas, data types, and prop definitions. Read references for real project data — product catalogs, collection schemas.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-workflow-step glass-panel">
              <div class="docs-workflow-number">3</div>
              <h3>Execute</h3>
              <p>Write code that follows the contracts. Run CLI commands like <code>jay-stack action</code> for live data discovery and code generation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-workflow-step glass-panel">
              <div class="docs-workflow-number">4</div>
              <h3>Validate</h3>
              <p>Run <code>jay-stack validate</code> to check correctness. When validation fails, the agent-kit guides explain the fix — a feedback loop back to the contracts and patterns.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section docs-roles">
        <div class="container">
          <div style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
            <span class="section-label">Guides</span>
            <h2 class="headline-lg" style="margin-top: 16px;">Browse by Role</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 24px; max-width: 700px; margin-top: 16px;">These guides are published here for the curious human. AI agents read them directly from the <code jay-design="allow" style="background: var(--color-surface-high); border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85em;">agent-kit/</code> folder in your project root, generated locally by the CLI.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="docs-roles-grid">
            <a class="docs-role-card glass-panel docs-role-card--designer" href="/docs/designer/instructions">
              <img class="docs-role-icon" src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_ebd9e460d96049b195b5ef0b340cffc8~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_80,h_80/file.webp" alt="Designer" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">
              <div class="docs-role-body">
                <h3>Designer</h3>
                <p>Creates <code>.jay-html</code> pages and templates. Binds to contract data using template syntax — data bindings, conditions, loops, and refs. Styles pages with CSS.</p>
                <span class="docs-role-link">25 guides &rarr;</span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="docs-role-card glass-panel docs-role-card--developer" href="/docs/developer/instructions">
              <img class="docs-role-icon" src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_838a1a4885714dae9579fe0b4d1a2293~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_80,h_80/file.webp" alt="Developer" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">
              <div class="docs-role-body">
                <h3>Developer</h3>
                <p>Creates page components, defines page contracts, configures routing, and sets up project services. Builds the full-stack logic — unburdened from HTML or CSS.</p>
                <span class="docs-role-link">13 guides &rarr;</span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="docs-role-card glass-panel docs-role-card--plugin" href="/docs/plugin/instructions">
              <img class="docs-role-icon" src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_e235dbf4943c4208aba88b4ed6ddd402~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_80,h_80/file.webp" alt="Plugin Developer" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">
              <div class="docs-role-body">
                <h3>Plugin Developer</h3>
                <p>Creates reusable headless components packaged as plugins. Defines contracts, actions, services, and CLI commands that other projects consume.</p>
                <span class="docs-role-link">20 guides &rarr;</span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="docs-role-card glass-panel docs-role-card--devops" href="/docs/devops/instructions">
              <img class="docs-role-icon" src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_eaf3402bcc7c4fc784b5ae848a04af28~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_80,h_80/file.webp" alt="DevOps" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">
              <div class="docs-role-body">
                <h3>DevOps</h3>
                <p>Handles production builds, deployment configuration, serving modes, and cache invalidation. Manages the Two-Server Architecture.</p>
                <span class="docs-role-link">6 guides &rarr;</span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="docs-role-card glass-panel docs-role-card--contracts" href="/docs/contracts/guide">
              <img class="docs-role-icon" src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/c569b3_28d5b6b49bd14042b0eae9070028acf6~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_80,h_80/file.webp" alt="Contracts" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy">
              <div class="docs-role-body">
                <h3>Contracts</h3>
                <p>The central binding concept. Contracts are the source of truth that connects plugin logic to designer templates — the agent-kit materializes them into a discoverable form. Covers YAML syntax, page and component contracts, linked contracts, and graduated examples.</p>
                <span class="docs-role-link">5 guides &rarr;</span>
              </div>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="docs-extensibility">
            <p><strong>Extensible by plugins.</strong> The agent-kit isn't static framework docs — plugins can extend it with their own role-specific guides. When you install a plugin, its guides are automatically included in the kit alongside the framework's own documentation, growing the kit with your project.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <jay:SiteFooter />
  </div>
</body>
</html>
